// Mutation testing of antevemus/aspecification-revolt (1.0.0): the whole src/ (three classes). Runs in the
// scheduled workflow (.github/workflows/quality.yml) with a coverage driver (pcov); locally:
//
//   XDEBUG_MODE=off vendor/bin/infection --threads=max --only-covering-test-cases \
//       --initial-tests-php-options="-d pcov.enabled=1 -d pcov.directory=$PWD/src"
//
// (where Xdebug is loaded twice, with a PHP_INI_SCAN_DIR that leaves its ini out).
// The group "http" (tests/Http: the proof of gain and the HTTP parity) is left out: it measures wall-clock time
// against a local server, so under the parallel load of a mutation run a slow machine could "kill" a mutant by
// a timing miss; every line of src/ is also covered by tests/Unit and tests/Property.
//
// Measured on 2026-10-20 (1.0.0 against ASpecification 2.6.0, Infection 0.35.8, PHP 8.4.13 with pcov): 121
// mutants, 115 killed, 2 errors (detected), 0 time-outs, 4 escaped, all equivalent (in RevoltRunner, the same
// three as in antevemus/alinq-revolt: a cancel() whose DeferredCancellation destructor cancels anyway, an
// unsubscribe() of a cancellation released with the task, a finally whose catch (Throwable) already receives
// every exception; in RevoltStageTransport, `<` turned into `<=` against the core's minimum budget, two values
// of a monotonic clock never equal in practice); MSI 96.69%, covered-code MSI 96.69%, mutation code coverage
// 100%. The minimum scores are one integer point below.
{
    "$schema": "vendor/infection/infection/resources/schema.json",
    "source": {
        "directories": ["src"]
    },
    "timeout": 60,
    "logs": {
        "text": "coverage/infection/infection.log",
        "summary": "coverage/infection/summary.log",
        "json": "coverage/infection/infection.json",
        "perMutator": "coverage/infection/per-mutator.md"
    },
    "tmpDir": "coverage/infection/tmp",
    "phpUnit": {
        "configDir": "."
    },
    "testFrameworkOptions": "--exclude-group=http",
    "minMsi": 95,
    "minCoveredMsi": 95,
    "mutators": {
        "@default": true
    }
}
